paragraph:
2-97. Simplify each radical expression.
a. (3\sqrt{2})^2
b. \sqrt{9/4}
c. \sqrt{1/3}
d. (3 + \sqrt{2})^2

2-113. Solve each equation for x (that is, put it in x = ___ form).
a. y = 2(x - 17)^2
b. y + 7 = \sqrt[3]{x + 5}

2-115. Write each expression below in simplest radical form.
a. \sqrt{75} + \sqrt{27}
b. \sqrt{x} + 2\sqrt{x}
c. (\sqrt{12})^2
d. (3\sqrt{12})^2

C-59. Graph the piecewise function f(x) = {
2^x if x ≥ 0
|x| if x < 0
}.

Here are some exercises to try. For problems 1 through 12, rewrite each expression. For problems 13 through 24, simplify each expression. You should not need a calculator for any of these problems.
1. x^{-5}
2. m^0
3. 4^{-1}
4. \sqrt[3]{y}
5. 1/(c^4)
6. 1/(b^{-2})
7. 12^{1/12}
8. z^{-3/4}
9. 1/((\sqrt[6]{7})^5)
10. 0^0
11. 9^{1/2}
12. \sqrt[5]{a^3}
13. (f^3)\sqrt[3]{f^3}
14. (1/27)^{-1/3}
15. (v^2 g^{3/4})^8
16. (1/(q^6))^7
17. d^{-9} d^{-4}
18. (3x w^4)^{-2}
19. (u^3 r^{-4})^{-2}
20. n^3(n^2)^5
21. 4(\sqrt{4})^4
22. 6(k^{1/2} t^5)^2
23. p^{15} p^{-15}
24. h^8 s^{12}(\sqrt[8]{h})(s^{1/4})
